{"compatibility":"minor","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: minor.

Protected data: `Y`.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

Changes: added an explicit prior `x_change ~ uniform(min(x), max(x));` before `x_change` is used in the model block. This represents the bounded parameter's implicit flat prior on its declared finite support as a built-in sampling statement, satisfying SafeStan's requirement that every parameter have exactly one prior before use. No data fields were added or changed. `N` and `x` remain unprotected context inputs.
","model_safe_stan":"data {
  int<lower=0> N;
  array[N] real x;
  array[N] real Y;
}
parameters {
  real<lower=0> sigma;
  real<lower=0> alpha;
  array[2] real beta;
  real<lower=min(x), upper=max(x)> x_change;
}
model {
  array[N] real mu;

  alpha ~ normal(0, 5);
  beta ~ normal(0, 5);
  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 5);
  x_change ~ uniform(min(x), max(x));

  for (n in 1 : N) {
    mu[n] = alpha
            + ((x[n] < x_change) ? beta[1] : beta[2]) * (x[n] - x_change);
  }

  Y ~ normal(mu, sigma);
}
","data_safe_json":"{"N":2,"Y":[2.376322872738066,5.414735034652741],"x":[5.69255264345685,4.751369227050612]}","protected_variables":["Y"]}
